1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,586
Meetings shouldn't end with notes.

2
00:00:04,636 --> 00:00:09,905
They should end with work getting done.

3
00:00:09,955 --> 00:00:11,950
This is Meetos.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,016
Every meeting creates promises: who
will do what, and by when.

5
00:00:16,066 --> 00:00:17,458
Most of them get lost.

6
00:00:17,508 --> 00:00:22,704
Meetos remembers every commitment and follows
it across meetings, until a person

7
00:00:22,754 --> 00:00:23,950
confirms it's done.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,342
You can record a meeting live, with
everyone's consent, or upload a transcript.

9
00:00:31,392 --> 00:00:36,207
Here's a forty-minute launch
review with six people.

10
00:00:36,257 --> 00:00:39,950
Meetos finds the speakers automatically.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,950
Analysis runs through Firebase AI
Logic hybrid inference.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,003
When this device can run Gemini Nano,
the transcript never leaves it.

13
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:54,599
Otherwise Gemini in the cloud takes over.

14
00:00:54,649 --> 00:00:58,897
Every part is labelled with
where it really ran —

15
00:00:58,947 --> 00:00:59,950
no guessing.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,917
Out come decisions, commitments,
owners and deadlines.

17
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:09,453
'By Friday' becomes a real date.

18
00:01:09,503 --> 00:01:18,624
Every item quotes the exact line it came from,
and anything the AI can't back up is

19
00:01:18,674 --> 00:01:19,950
thrown away.

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,425
This is the Commitment Graph.

21
00:01:24,475 --> 00:01:36,617
Meetos linked this meeting to promises from
the last two weeks: a deadline that

22
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:44,950
moved, a blocker, and a task
someone says is finished.

23
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,640
But the AI never closes a task.

24
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:51,260
A person confirms it —

25
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:54,950
and the database enforces that.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,368
Decisions are remembered too: who agreed, and
when a later decision replaced an

27
00:02:05,418 --> 00:02:06,950
earlier one.

28
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,580
Ask your meetings anything.

29
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:14,450
Answers come only from your
records, with sources.

30
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:21,950
And if it was never discussed, Meetos says
so instead of making something up.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:32,156
Before the next meeting, Meetos prepares a
briefing: what's overdue, what's blocked,

32
00:02:32,206 --> 00:02:34,950
and a suggested agenda.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,426
Execution shows how commitments are
really going, from real records —

34
00:02:40,476 --> 00:02:44,950
and the Daily Brief tells you what
needs attention today.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,165
You choose where AI runs.

36
00:02:47,215 --> 00:02:51,950
On-device only means nothing is
sent to a cloud model.

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,495
Meetos.

38
00:02:52,545 --> 00:02:55,690
Meetings that end with work getting done.

39
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,950
Built with Firebase AI Logic.
